    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total now drop the single highest and single lowest person's figure when three or more people have one. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**Server** (`RollupService.java`): it now collects each person's figure and adds them up through a new `trimmedTotal` helper. A due-total of n/a isn't collected at all, so it never counts as a figure. Every person's overdue-total is collected. Because the `TOTALS` audit line reads these totals, it is trimmed too, with no other changes.\n\n**Front end**: I added `trimmedTotal` next to the existing `total` in `features/rates/rates.ts` and switched only the three sheet-level displays to it:\n- `DueTotal.tsx` (`rollup-due-total`)\n- `OverdueTotals.tsx` (`rollup-overdue-total`)\n- `HeaderCounters.tsx` (`header-due-total`, `header-overdue-total`)\n\nEverything else still uses the untrimmed `total`: per-person figures, per-grade and per-period totals, backing, the claimed total, and the overdue count.",
